From 3d39facf521b22fdf8d54327035ceb860fcc5267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Upstream Contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:21:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(metrics): add a multilingual refusal scorer and detector

RefusalDetector matches eight English regexes, and its `can'?t` misses the
curly apostrophe models often emit. A refusal in any other language scores
as "did not refuse", so refusal rates on multilingual safety sets are wrong.

Add refusal phrases for English, Hindi, Hinglish, Bengali, Tamil, Arabic
and Swahili, exposed as ak.multilingual_refusal (an @ak.scorer, with
ak.refusal_scorer for another name or direction) and as the
refusal_multilingual red-team detector.

Text is NFC-normalised, curly apostrophes fold to straight ones and
zero-width joiners are dropped, so the encoding of a phrase can't hide it.
English is always checked too, because models often switch to it to refuse.

The language comes from sample.metadata["lang"] or sample.task. A language
with no patterns is reported as not_tested and left out of the aggregate,
because a 0.0 there would read as a failed refusal.

RefusalDetector itself is unchanged.
